            {
                "entry_id": "d8e4c54a-d8e8-3c94-accb-a3909018990e",
                "word": "Stakhanovite",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "940b7c0e-bac5-4b34-ba04-fd6900906468",
                        "entry_id": "d8e4c54a-d8e8-3c94-accb-a3909018990e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "Stakhanovites"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "cdd68000-12cd-3c81-9f65-98278427d693",
                        "entry_id": "d8e4c54a-d8e8-3c94-accb-a3909018990e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An extremely productive or hard-working worker, especially in the former USSR, who may earn special rewards; a workaholic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "historical"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69c5c7a4-7933-40d6-be3b-6f7896162602",
                                "sense_id": "cdd68000-12cd-3c81-9f65-98278427d693",
                                "text": "Nevertheless, few outstanding Stakhanovites remained at the bench for very long. Even if they stayed on the enterprise payroll, they ceased to be workers, becoming instead living icons."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "45862de5-bb31-4904-a964-1e8fdd627dfb",
                                "sense_id": "cdd68000-12cd-3c81-9f65-98278427d693",
                                "text": "Kolkhozniki were soon attacking the Stakhanovites with abandon, beating them up, destroying their animals, even killing them.⁴⁰ For obvious reasons, collective farm management and even village authorities were often also not eager to see labor norms increased and colluded in these attacks."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7d433fd1-3b78-48e1-a976-441cf1151c1d",
                                "sense_id": "cdd68000-12cd-3c81-9f65-98278427d693",
                                "text": "In mid-1936, the steel plant's deputy director, Khazanov, revealed that according to factory administration data there were 3,663 Stackhanovites at the steel plant, but according to the records of the trade union committee, there were 4,441. “In our shops,” he commented, “there are insufficiently precise criteria for determining Stakhanovites.”"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
